  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: High pressure system continues to\nstrengthen over the southwest which will continue to bring in\nwarmer temperatures and keep weather conditions dry. Warming\ntemperature trends will make most of northern central Nevada be\nseveral degrees above normal with near record temperatures on\nFriday, Saturday, and Sunday afternoons. Each major city in\ncentral and northern Nevada will see above 80 degrees with a\n70-90% chance of reaching up to 85 degrees (with the exception of\nEly and Eureka seeing a 10-50% chance of reaching above 80\ndegrees). Slightly cooler temperatures expected on Monday, but\nwith highs still remaining several degrees above normal with parts\nof northern Nevada seeing near record temperatures. Tuesday and\nthrough the rest of the week, temperatures cool into the upper 70s\nfor most parts with a few spots in western Nevada staying in the\n80s. \n\nA weak upper trough is expected to move over northern Nevada early\nnext week, however the system is expected to be very dry giving\nzero chance of any precipitation in the silver state. The system\nis what weakens the high pressure system slightly which will stop\nthe gradual warming for next week and keep high temperatures in\nthe upper 70s to 80s. Generally light winds expected throughout\nthe forecast period.",
